From 43a739c871e6cf0e0e2489324ed682b2dca09fc2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ROCKNIX Project <dev@rocknix.org>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 17:07:05 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] leds: rgb: add AYANEO serial MCU support

Bind the AYANEO serial MCU as the sole serdev owner of its dedicated UART.
On the Pocket EVO, expose the two four-zone stick rings through eight
multicolor LED class devices and a versioned, atomic device-level sysfs ABI.

Implement the physically validated broadcast, per-ring, and direct-zone
register frames, autonomous Rainbow and Reactive initializers, host-rendered
Breath modes, exact shutdown, optional Xbox 360 controller-mode bootstrap,
and suspend-safe state restoration. Only send the controller-mode sequence
when the ayaneo,xbox360-mode property is present. All traffic and cached state
share one mutex, and synchronous writes handle partial UART acceptance.

Apply the device-tuned red-aware colour calibration only while serializing
user RGB values. Expose ABI revision 3 so applications can atomically tune
the device-wide green and blue percentages without corrupting semantic
caches.
---
